        {
          "type": "note",
          "name": "Behaviour — branch scope picker",
          "x": -4040,
          "y": 800,
          "width": 470,
          "height": 400,
          "content": "Branch scope picker — replaces the native Select\n\n• The scope button sits first in the Log filter bar and names what the log shows: “All branches”, or the picked ref’s last path segment, with ✕ to clear.\n• Pressing it opens the picker inline under the bar (no popover: the pane has none, and nothing gets clipped). The log stays visible but faded.\n• Typing filters every ref as you type (substring, case-insensitive); the matching part is highlighted.\n• Sections: LOCAL, REMOTE ONLY (remotes whose local copy exists fold into the local row as ⇅), TAGS. Each shows 5 rows then “+n more · type to narrow”.\n• Rows: kind icon in the kind colour, the prefix dim and the tail strong, ↑↓ ahead/behind, age, ✓ on the current scope.\n• Quick scopes: All branches · Current branch · Local only.\n• Picking a ref closes the picker and reloads the log; Done or the button closes without change.\n• Branches tab reuses the same rows; Terminal falls back to the same list as plain text buttons.",
          "id": "lcLpV"
        }
      ],
      "x": 4040,
      "y": 0
    }
  ],
